1
00:00:00,148 --> 00:00:03,337
Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:05,358
If you're new here, welcome.

3
00:00:05,358 --> 00:00:09,307
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

4
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:16,288
One of the most talked-about AI companies in the world has just asked to be listed

5
00:00:16,288 --> 00:00:17,089
on the stock market.

6
00:00:17,089 --> 00:00:18,900
And its paperwork shows something strange:

7
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:24,000
it made about sixteen billion dollars in six months, and still lost about eighty.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,544
How does that happen?

9
00:00:25,544 --> 00:00:28,923
And what does the company itself say could go wrong?

10
00:00:29,652 --> 00:00:31,184
Hi, I'm Mittal Shah.

11
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:35,032
The company is Anthropic, the maker of the Claude AI models.

12
00:00:35,032 --> 00:00:36,268
Here is what happened.

13
00:00:36,268 --> 00:00:42,785
On the twenty-sixth of October, it publicly filed its registration document with the

14
00:00:42,785 --> 00:00:44,886
United States regulator.

15
00:00:44,886 --> 00:00:47,448
The document is called an S-1.

16
00:00:47,448 --> 00:00:52,003
It is the form a company files to sell shares to the public for the first time,

17
00:00:52,003 --> 00:00:54,168
which is what an I-P-O is.

18
00:00:54,168 --> 00:00:58,328
The company says it wants its shares listed on the Nasdaq exchange, under the ticker

19
00:00:58,328 --> 00:00:59,944
A-N-T.

20
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:02,161
Now, what has not happened.

21
00:01:02,161 --> 00:01:04,650
The document is filed, but not yet effective.

22
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:07,231
Until it is, no shares can be sold.

23
00:01:07,231 --> 00:01:13,314
It does not say how many shares will be offered, at what price, or on which date.

24
00:01:13,314 --> 00:01:17,651
Press reports say the sale could come in the next few weeks, but that is not

25
00:01:17,651 --> 00:01:18,326
confirmed.

26
00:01:18,957 --> 00:01:20,788
So, what do the numbers show?

27
00:01:20,788 --> 00:01:25,374
For the first six months of this year, the filing reports revenue of about sixteen

28
00:01:25,374 --> 00:01:26,798
point three billion dollars.

29
00:01:26,798 --> 00:01:31,545
It also reports a net loss of about eighty point seven billion dollars.

30
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,879
Why is the loss so much bigger than the revenue?

31
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:40,045
The reports on the filing say it comes mostly from changes in the value of

32
00:01:40,045 --> 00:01:42,004
convertible notes and similar instruments.

33
00:01:42,004 --> 00:01:48,248
A convertible note is money lent to a company, with the right to turn it into shares

34
00:01:48,248 --> 00:01:48,848
later.

35
00:01:48,722 --> 00:01:51,453
Think of it like a coupon for shares.

36
00:01:51,453 --> 00:01:57,882
If the company becomes more valuable, each coupon is worth more, and the company has

37
00:01:57,882 --> 00:01:59,678
to record that rise as a cost.

38
00:01:59,678 --> 00:02:02,530
It is an accounting entry, not cash going out the door.

39
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:05,752
That is why the loss is described as largely non-cash.

40
00:02:06,322 --> 00:02:09,028
Now, the part that deserves the most attention:

41
00:02:09,028 --> 00:02:09,628
the risks.

42
00:02:09,488 --> 00:02:13,633
A company going public must warn investors about what could go wrong.

43
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:18,767
The risk section of this filing runs to more than ninety pages, far longer than

44
00:02:18,767 --> 00:02:19,367
most.

45
00:02:18,997 --> 00:02:20,873
Here are four of the warnings.

46
00:02:21,545 --> 00:02:22,825
First, safety.

47
00:02:22,825 --> 00:02:27,092
The company writes that advanced AI could pose, and I quote, "catastrophic or

48
00:02:27,092 --> 00:02:34,613
existential risks to humanity", especially if it is misused, turned into a weapon,

49
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:36,625
or left to act with a high degree of autonomy.

50
00:02:36,625 --> 00:02:42,100
It warns that autonomous systems could take harmful actions on their own and at

51
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:42,700
scale.

52
00:02:42,622 --> 00:02:48,697
And it says that no single insurer, and perhaps not even the whole insurance

53
00:02:48,697 --> 00:02:53,587
industry, may have the capacity to cover a catastrophe like that.

54
00:02:53,587 --> 00:02:57,382
These are the company's own words to investors, not our view.

55
00:02:57,905 --> 00:02:59,180
Second, computing power.

56
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:04,343
Training and running these models needs enormous amounts of specialised computing.

57
00:03:04,343 --> 00:03:09,730
Reports on the filing say the company has committed to spend more than five hundred

58
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:11,077
billion dollars on it.

59
00:03:11,077 --> 00:03:16,016
The filing warns that this spending comes before the revenue it is meant to earn.

60
00:03:16,016 --> 00:03:19,450
This could mean that if demand falls short, the bills still arrive.

61
00:03:20,176 --> 00:03:21,562
Third, governments.

62
00:03:21,562 --> 00:03:27,317
The reports say the United States government has labelled the company a national

63
00:03:27,317 --> 00:03:33,831
security supply-chain risk, after a dispute over limits the company set on military

64
00:03:33,831 --> 00:03:35,213
use of its models.

65
00:03:35,213 --> 00:03:37,575
The company is challenging that in court.

66
00:03:37,575 --> 00:03:41,294
And in June, export restrictions forced it to switch off two of its models for all

67
00:03:41,294 --> 00:03:46,288
customers, before bringing them back with updated safeguards.

68
00:03:46,947 --> 00:03:47,633
Fourth, control.

69
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:53,174
The filing names the co-founders, Dario Amodei and Daniela Amodei, as critical, and

70
00:03:53,174 --> 00:03:55,690
says they would be difficult to replace.

71
00:03:55,690 --> 00:04:00,492
Reports say seven co-founders will hold a special class of shares carrying fifty

72
00:04:00,492 --> 00:04:06,049
point one per cent of the votes, and an independent trust picks a majority of the

73
00:04:06,049 --> 00:04:06,649
board.

74
00:04:06,276 --> 00:04:12,184
The filing itself warns that this structure may effectively remove the ability of

75
00:04:12,184 --> 00:04:16,274
ordinary shareholders to influence important decisions.

76
00:04:16,893 --> 00:04:19,596
That is why this listing is so unusual:

77
00:04:19,596 --> 00:04:24,415
the company is telling the public, in a legal document, that its own technology

78
00:04:24,415 --> 00:04:25,394
could be dangerous.

79
00:04:25,948 --> 00:04:28,827
There is a link to an earlier story of ours.

80
00:04:28,827 --> 00:04:33,382
On the twenty-sixth of October, in the episode "Big AI spending:

81
00:04:33,382 --> 00:04:39,376
when does it pay back?", we looked at the huge sums the big technology companies are

82
00:04:39,376 --> 00:04:42,084
spending on computing power for AI.

83
00:04:42,084 --> 00:04:43,838
The link is in the description.

84
00:04:44,494 --> 00:04:46,144
What do we not know yet?

85
00:04:46,144 --> 00:04:51,056
The share price, the number of shares, the date, and the final version of the

86
00:04:51,056 --> 00:04:51,656
numbers.

87
00:04:51,485 --> 00:04:54,903
The filing can change before it becomes effective.

88
00:04:55,551 --> 00:04:56,500
To sum up:

89
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:00,326
a leading AI lab is about to open its books for the first time.

90
00:05:00,326 --> 00:05:04,611
The headline loss is mostly an accounting entry, not cash spent.

91
00:05:04,611 --> 00:05:09,802
The bigger story is the risk list, where the company itself says the stakes are

92
00:05:09,802 --> 00:05:10,402
high.

93
00:05:10,627 --> 00:05:14,163
This is news and explanation, not investment advice.

94
00:05:14,163 --> 00:05:17,112
Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

